# T-2071 companion: outer 'env' binding is NOT referenced from the final expression.
# 'result' references the inner 'env' (shadowed by the second dict), not the outer one.
# The outer 'env' from the first dict should produce a lost-binding warning.
# BindingId (span-keyed) must distinguish the outer 'env' (source span 1) from any
# inner binding with the same name, so only the outer one is flagged.
[call [fn [let x]
  [env: x]
  [env: "shadowed"]
  env]
"hello"]
=== out
String("shadowed")

=== warn
variable 'env' is never referenced
